    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3863300": {
      "title": "Assumption University Staff - Graduate Assistant Athletics Communications",
      "description": "Assumption University Staff - Graduate Assistant Athletics Communications In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Assumption University Staff > Graduate Assistant Athletics Communications Assumption University Staff Apply Graduate Assistant Athletics Communications Worcester, MA Apply Description BASIC PURPOSE: Assists in the development and management of a comprehensive NCAA Division II athletics program as a member of the athletics management team in support of the mission of the University. Primary responsibilities are to serve as liaison between the University Community, the media and the general public with regards to intercollegiate sports programs in an effort to obtain positive and frequent media coverage of all athletics programs. This is a 20 hour per week, 40 week/year position.  Compensation includes tuition in an Assumption University graduate program for a total of 8 courses per academic year, with a recommended schedule of 3 courses in the fall, 3 in the spring, and 2 in the summer. Tuition Remission does not include fees.  Cannot be combined with other positions at the University. ACCOUNTABILITIES: Serve as primary contact to multiple sports for contest coverage, website information, game notes, statistics, and media relations. Writes and submits news releases, and informs media regarding newsworthy items. Compiles accurate statistics for student-athletes and teams, and reports results to staff personnel and representatives. Oversees media coverage of games and game management for all sports (i.e., scorers, timers, other professional personnel). Maintains organized and accurate historical records using current technology. Maintains all aspects of photography (i.e., team/individual photographs, all special events) by using current technology. Record and edit video highlight packages Manages and updates the department web site, providing data and materials for general viewing and up-to-date scores and schedules, rosters, and historical materials by understanding and utilizing the most current technology. Facilitate and provide content on various social media platforms. Assists in the coordination of all media and marketing publications related responsibilities for the regular events (i.e. athletics contests) and special events (i.e. dinners, awards night, tournaments, etc.). Prioritize attendance at University events such as: Student/athlete Candlelight, Hall of Fame Dinner, Athletics Awards Night, Orientation, Graduation, etc. Performs other related duties as assigned by the Assistant Director of Athletics for Communications. Responsible for the oversight and implementation of the Department’s comprehensive video production and film exchange programs. SCOPE: Maintains on-going contacts with representatives of the various media outlets. Communicates regularly with University students, faculty and staff. Maintains extensive photographic and video library of all student/athletes – past and present. Prepares and submits news releases throughout the year. Possesses and understands the many skills required for the profession; i.e., journalistic, graphic design, photographic, videotape and electronic media, computer program, application and networking. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  Sitting, standing, walking, and bending are required of this position. This position requires working nights and weekends. Use of a computer keyboard and computer screen for periods of time with close vision and the ability to adjust visual focus plus manual dexterity are required. MENTAL DEMANDS: The mental demands described are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  Examples of mental demands include reading (documents), detailed work, confidentiality, language, math, reasoning, oral communications, written communications, customer contact, multiple concurrent tasks, constant interruptions, and performing calculations when necessary. ABOUT ASSUMPTION UNIVERSITY: St. John Paul II wrote: “Man’s creation by God ‘in his own image’ confers upon every human person an eminent dignity; it also postulates the fundamental equality of all human beings.” Assumption University recognizes the essential contribution of a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty and condemns all forms of harassment, discrimination, and disrespect. As such, and in compliance with the requirements of federal law and/or the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Assumption University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, and pregnancy, as well as other legally protected status, in admission to, access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, except where such conditions may constitute bona fide qualifications for the programs or activities in question. * Requirements QUALIFICATIONS Must be willing to contribute actively to the mission of the University as well as show respect for the Catholic and Assumptionist identity of Assumption Must be a current graduate student at Assumption University in good academic standing. Bachelor’s degree and 1-3 years customer service or administrative experience required. Internship experience may be substituted for work experience. Strong time, project management, and organization skills; strong attention to detail. Strong analytical and problem solving skills. Ability to be proactive, innovative and creative. Ability to work evening and weekend hours. Strong written and oral communication and public relations, management and leadership skills. Proficient in use of current technology. Candidates with knowledge and skill in Adobe Creative Suite, Final Cut Pro, Stat Crew and Presto Sports website management will be given highest priority Salary Description $15 *an hour Apply Assumption University Staff Jobs View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    }
